The HubInvocationContext constructor requires a Hub and MethodInfo and a list of method arguments, which I need to provide. I will try to find the HubInvocationContext type in the Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR namespace or assembly, as it is part of SignalR. I will read the Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR package source or try to mock the HubInvocationContext with the required parameters.

I will try to create a minimal Hub subclass and use reflection to get a MethodInfo for a method to pass to the HubInvocationContext constructor. This will allow me to construct the HubInvocationContext properly for the test.

I will resubmit the test with these fixes. I will also remove the test for the protected method since it is inaccessible and the refactor to make it virtual was not possible.

